ic dynein is required for flagellar assembly.</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><volume>144</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>481</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9971742</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005384-Hou1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hou</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Pazour</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Witman</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>A dynein light intermediate chain, D1bLIC, is required for retrograde intraflagellar transport.</article-title><source>Mol Biol Cell</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>4382</fpage><lpage>4394</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15269286</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005384-Cole2"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The intraflagellar transport machinery of <italic>Chlamydomonas</italic> reinhardtii.</article-title><source>Traffic</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>442</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12795688</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005384-Piperno1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Piperno</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mead</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Transport of a novel complex in the cytoplasmic matrix of <italic>Chlamydomonas</italic> flagella.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>94</volume><fpage>4457</fpage><lpage>4462</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9114011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005384-Qin1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name